<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Unitarian Party</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Unitarian Party was a political faction in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a> in the decades after independence that favoured a centralised state led from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>, liberal reforms and European-style institutions. Its leaders included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardino-rivadavia">Bernardino Rivadavia</a> and General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-paz">José María Paz</a>. In the civil wars against the Federalists, especially under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/juan-manuel-de-rosas">Juan Manuel de Rosas</a>, many Unitarians were killed or driven into exile, and their cause later merged into the liberal nation-building of the 1850s and 1860s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/unitarian-party.jpg" alt="Unitarian Party" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Unitarian_Party_(Navy).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
